<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thorfinn the Mighty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1009–c. 1065</span> · Also known as Thorfinn Sigurdsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thorfinn the Mighty (c. 1009–c. 1065) was Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> and a grandson, through his mother, of the Scottish king Malcolm II. After a long struggle with his nephew Rögnvald Brusason he ruled all of Orkney and, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkneyinga-saga">Orkneyinga saga</a>, extended his power over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shetland">Shetland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caithness">Caithness</a> and parts of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a>. He built a minster at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birsay">Birsay</a>.</p></div>
